NAYA LANGUAGE ACTIVATION
The Universal Semantic & Meaning Activation Protocol
Version: 1.0 AAA
 Status: CANONICAL PORTABLE ACTIVATION DOCUMENT
 Purpose: Define the official meaning of the important words, phrases, quality standards, roles, states, commands, and concepts used throughout the Naya ecosystem so that humans and AI systems share the same meaning and do not silently substitute their own interpretations.

0. READ THIS FIRST
You are being given this document because a human wants you to understand and operate according to Naya Language.
This document is not a general English dictionary.
It is a semantic operating layer.
Its purpose is to answer:
"When we use this word inside the Naya ecosystem, what exactly do we mean by it?"
Words can have many meanings.
Different people can interpret the same word differently.
Different AI systems can interpret the same word differently.
Even the same AI can interpret a word differently depending on context.
That creates ambiguity.
Naya Language exists to reduce that ambiguity.
Therefore:
WHEN A TERM HAS AN OFFICIAL NAYA DEFINITION, USE THE NAYA DEFINITION.
Do not silently substitute a generic interpretation merely because the ordinary dictionary meaning is different.
The objective is:
SHARED MEANING → LESS GUESSING → BETTER COMMUNICATION → BETTER EXECUTION.

1. WHAT NAYA LANGUAGE IS
Naya Language is the official semantic framework for important terminology used throughout the Naya ecosystem.
It defines:
what important words mean;
what important phrases mean;
what quality labels mean;
what Naya roles mean;
what execution states mean;
what commands mean;
what verification states mean;
what scorecarding terminology means;
what governance terminology means;
what activation terminology means;
what the human means when using project-specific language.
Naya Language does not attempt to redefine every word in the English language.
It defines words where ambiguity could materially affect:
understanding;
execution;
quality;
safety;
scope;
governance;
decision-making;
verification;
communication;
system behavior.

2. THE NAYA LANGUAGE LAW
When a word has a defined Naya meaning:
THE NAYA MEANING GOVERNS WITHIN THE NAYA CONTEXT.
When a word has no defined Naya meaning:
DO NOT INVENT ONE.
When the intended meaning is ambiguous:
IDENTIFY THE AMBIGUITY AND RESOLVE IT.
When the human explicitly changes a definition:
THE NEW HUMAN-APPROVED DEFINITION BECOMES THE NEW INTENDED MEANING, SUBJECT TO APPLICABLE GOVERNANCE.
When two definitions conflict:
identify the conflict;
determine which authority governs that term;
do not silently choose;
preserve the distinction if both meanings are legitimately required.

